BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JCW: One Mic Stand with SJ
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260814T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260814T220000
UID:81b52703ad5227153d2bd54d7a653838@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Step up. Speak out. Stand tall. Jersey City Writers invites yo
 u to One-Mic Stand with SJ—an open mic experience like no other! This is
  where raw talent meets electrifying energy\, and every voice has a chance
  to shine. On the 2nd Friday of every month\, two incredible featured poet
 s will take the stage alongside a lineup of fearless performers from our v
 ibrant poetry community. Open mic slots are 5 minutes each\, giving you th
 e perfect space to share your truth—whether it’s poetry\, spoken word\
 , or a story waiting to be heard. Come for the poetry. Stay for the magic.
  Join the movement. $10 Suggested Donation (Cash\, Venmo\, Paypal) Doors o
 pen at 6:30pm\, Open Mic starts at 7pm -- first come\, first served! Our H
 ost Steve Willett (SJ) is a sound poet who is actively involved in the poe
 try community and has had several feature performances around New Jersey. 
 His poem ‘Petulance’ was a shortlisted selection for the University of
  Grimsby’s Hammond House International Poetry Competition in 2019. Steve
  serves as moderator for the Jersey City Writers (JC Plums) poetry group\,
  which meets online every week to discuss poetry and improve participants'
  works. He was also one of the producers for the Jersey City Writers JC Po
 etry Festival in 2023 and is currently working on the 2025 festival. He is
  also a teaching artist at Newark School of the Arts. He lives with his wi
 fe\, 2 daughters\, and 5 cats in the Heights. He is excited to have his ow
 n Open Mic\, (One-Mic Stand with SJ)\, and give back to a community that h
 as given so much support to him. 08/14 FEATURED ACTS: Noah Arhm Choi &amp\
 ; Meliq the Plant Poet Noah Arhm Choi is the author of Cut to Bloom\, winn
 er of the 2019 Jack McCarthy Prize. A Lambda Literary Poet-In-Residence an
 d Valentines Editor for Honey Literary\, they received an MFA from Sarah L
 awrence\, and their work appears in The Adroit Journal\, Split this Rock\,
  The Rumpus\, Foglifter\, and elsewhere. Noah was shortlisted for the Poet
 ry International Prize and received the Ellen Conroy Kennedy Poetry Prize\
 , alongside fellowships from Kundiman\, the Sewanee Writers’ Conference\
 , and the Adirondack Center for Writing. They serve on the Kundiman Board 
 of Trustees and currently work at NYU Metro Center for Research on Equity 
 and the Transformation of Schools. A K-12 educator of fifteen years\, they
  work to embolden the intersection of education\, activism\, and the arts.
  Meliq August aka Meliq the Plant Poet is a Belizean-American\, queer\, no
 n-binary\, multi-disciplinary artist\, earthworker\, budding herbalist\, a
 nd transformative educator. Hailing from North Bergen\, NJ\, they are now 
 paving the way with their robust talents in the city of Newark through hea
 ling avenues stemming from an Afro-Indigenous framework of thought. With a
  collegiate background in sociology and photography\, Meliq focuses on the
  intersectionality of identity as well as their lanes of expertise to shak
 e and make a difference in the community. Through their artistry and activ
 ism\, Meliq strongly focuses on the upliftment and empowerment of Black\, 
 Indigenous\, Trans\, and Queer peoples\, as well as all other historically
  marginalized communities. To connect or learn more about their work\, the
 y can be contacted through instagram @meliqaugust or via email at [meliq.a
 ugust@gmail.com](mailto:meliq.august@gmail.com) Supported by public funds 
 from the Jersey City Arts and Culture Trust Fund THEME: OPEN MIC / FEATURE
 S HOST: JERSEY CITY WRITERS FEATURES: Noah Arhm Choi &amp\; Meliq August a
 ka Meliq the Plant Poet PRICE: $10 Suggested Donation (Cash\, Venmo\, Payp
 al) CONTACT: @jcwriters
LOCATION:156 1st St\, Jersey City\, NJ 07302
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/jcw-one-mic-stand-with-sj
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poets &amp\; Storytellers Open
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260814T185000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260814T210000
UID:f043a71e1510657264cdfe276af7267c@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:Name of Event: &nbsp\;Poets &amp\; Storytellers Open Date: &nb
 sp\;August 14\, 2026 Start/End Time: &nbsp\;6:50 PM - 9:00 PM Address: &nb
 sp\;Wull &amp\; Oak 10 E. Broad St. Hopewell\, NJ 08525 Theme: &nbsp\;Poet
 ry Open Mic Host: &nbsp\;Echo Thread Books Feature(s): &nbsp\;Isabel Cruz 
 Price: &nbsp\;Free Email Address: &nbsp\; EchoThreadPresents@gmail.com Web
 site: &nbsp\; http://www.echothreadprojects.com/poets-storytellers-open So
 cial Media: &nbsp\; @echothreadbooks Event Description: &nbsp\; Announcing
  our next Poets &amp\; Storytellers Open on August 14th! Join us for an ev
 ening of poetry and conversation at Wull &amp\; Oak in Downtown Hopewell. 
 P&amp\;SO welcomes everyone to bring their original poetry or prose\, poli
 shed or in progress\, to this wonderful space. P&amp\;SO is a space for wr
 iters performing or working out original pieces. The open mic signup list 
 caps off at 12 readers and does fill up quickly\, so be sure to arrive on 
 time to secure a spot! Each performer will have up to 5 minutes to share t
 heir work. For those who would only like to watch the performances\, you
 ’re more than welcome to also join our audience. The event is free and o
 pen for all to enjoy\, but we do welcome donations to help keep the event 
 funded. For August\, we’re very excited to welcome Isabel Cruz! Isabel (
  @eesahvel ) is a Puerto Rican poet and Emeritus Youth Poetry Ambassador f
 or the Paterson Poetry Festival\, and recipient of awards such as the 2024
  Five College Prose &amp\; Poetry Prize and the 2024 Elizabeth Babcock Pri
 ze for Best Poem. Her work is published or forthcoming with The Poetry Soc
 iety of New York\, I Feel Nothing Like Good Anthology\, Brooklyn Poets Poe
 t of the Week\, ART SICK\, By The WAYE\, and Acentos Review\, among others
 . A Q&amp\;A session will follow Isabel’s set. Details for the evening: 
 6:50 PM - doors/open mic signup begins* 7:15 to 8:15 PM - open mic 8:30 to
  9:00 PM - featured poet Wull &amp\; Oak is located at: 10 E. Broad St. Ho
 pewell\, NJ Light refreshments will be provided. See you there! *Please be
  mindful that W&amp\;O closes at 6PM on Friday evenings\, and we use the n
 ext 50 minutes to rearrange and set up the space before opening back up fo
 r the event. THEME: OPEN MIC / FEATURE HOST: Echo Thread Books FEATURES: T
 BA PRICE: FREE - http://www.echothreadprojects.com/poets-storytellers-open
  CONTACT: @echothreadbooks / EchoThreadPresents@gmail.com
LOCATION:Wull &amp\; Oak\, 10 East Broad Street\, Hopewell\, NJ\, 08525
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/poets-storytellers-open-aug
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
