BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:JERSEY CITY BOOK FAIR
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261003T170000
UID:3e648146e4bef0d392109ab406d17605@njpoetryevents.com
DESCRIPTION:We are so excited to officially invite you to be part of the&n
 bsp\; inaugural Jersey City Book Fair \, produced by&nbsp\; Marc Polite &n
 bsp\;and&nbsp\; Millicent Ansah ! Join us on&nbsp\; Saturday\, October 3\,
  from 12:00 PM–5:00 PM &nbsp\;at the&nbsp\; Bethune Center &nbsp\;(140 M
 artin Luther King Dr.\, Jersey City\, NJ 07305) as part of&nbsp\; JCAST (J
 ersey City Art &amp\; Studio Tour) &nbsp\;for a&nbsp\; FREE &nbsp\;celebra
 tion of literature\, storytelling\, and literacy. The Jersey City Book Fai
 r was created with a simple vision: to celebrate the power of books\, ampl
 ify diverse literary voices\, and create opportunities for readers\, write
 rs\, educators\, artists\, and community organizations to connect. We beli
 eve everyone deserves to see themselves reflected in the stories they read
 \, and we're excited to create a space where those stories can be shared a
 nd celebrated. We'd Love for You to Be Part of It! We're currently looking
  for: &nbsp\; Authors Especially local authors\, Black authors\, diasporic
  voices\, and writers from marginalized communities. &nbsp\; Children's Bo
 ok Authors To participate in our Children's Literacy Room and Children's L
 iteracy Panel Discussion. &nbsp\; Small Presses &amp\; Independent Publish
 ers &nbsp\; Literacy Organizations &amp\; Educational Resource Providers &
 nbsp\; Community Partners &nbsp\; Vendors &nbsp\; Panelists &amp\; Speaker
 s &nbsp\; Sponsors &amp\; Donors Whether you're sharing your latest book\,
  connecting families with literacy resources\, promoting your organization
 \, or supporting the event through sponsorship\, we'd be honored to have y
 ou join us in making this inaugural celebration something truly special. V
 endor Opportunities &nbsp\; Full Table: &nbsp\;$60 &nbsp\; Half Table: &nb
 sp\;$30 Vendor fees and donations directly support event logistics\, progr
 amming\, featured artists\, and operational costs\, helping us keep admiss
 ion&nbsp\; FREE &nbsp\;while investing in local authors and a thriving lit
 erary community. Get Involved &nbsp\; Reserve your vendor table and learn 
 more about the event here: Jersey City Book Fair Eventbrite Jersey City Bo
 ok Fair Vendor Form If you'd like to become a community partner\, serve as
  a speaker or panelist\, sponsor the event\, or have questions about parti
 cipating\, we'd love to hear from you. &nbsp\; Email us at: &nbsp\; bookfa
 irjc@gmail.com &nbsp\;Please find the event flyer attached and feel free t
 o share it with your networks\, colleagues\, friends\, and fellow book lov
 ers.&nbsp\; Stay Connected Follow the Jersey City Book Fair for event upda
 tes\, author announcements\, partnership opportunities\, and more! &nbsp\;
  Instagram: &nbsp\; @bookfairjc &nbsp\; Facebook: &nbsp\; Jersey City Book
  Fair &nbsp\; Website: &nbsp\; Jersey City Book Fair Website A heartfelt t
 hank you to our community partners: The Bethune Center Jersey City Free Pu
 blic Library Office of Cultural Affairs The Common Earth Company This proj
 ect is supported by the Jersey City Arts Council and the Jersey City Arts 
 &amp\; Culture Trust Fund. We're also grateful to Expressions by MowZus an
 d JPI Films\, who will be documenting this exciting inaugural event. Thank
  you for believing in the power of books\, stories\, and community. We hop
 e you'll join us on October 3 as we begin what we hope will become a cheri
 shed literary tradition in Jersey City. With gratitude\, Millicent Ansah&n
 bsp\; Co- Founder &amp\; Producer Jersey City Book Fair &nbsp\; bookfairjc
 @gmail.com THEME: BOOK FAIR HOST: Jersey City Book Fair FEATURES: Please r
 each out if you would like to be a vendor\, volunteer or speaker. PRICE: F
 REE / Full Table:&nbsp\;$60&nbsp\;Half / Table:&nbsp\;$30 - https://jersey
 citybookfair.wordpress.com/ / Jersey City Book Fair Vendor Form CONTACT: E
 mail us at bookfairjc@gmail.com / @bookfairjc / FB - Jersey City Book Fair
LOCATION:The Bethune Center\, 140 Martin Luther King Drive\, Jersey City\,
  NJ\, 07305
URL:https://www.njpoetryevents.com/calendar/jersey-city-book-fair
X-SOURCE:NJ Poetry Events
END:VEVENT
